1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,579
In Indonesia, a small fault on a motorbike or a water pump can cost a day's wage.

2
00:00:07,579 --> 00:00:12,292
Repair videos can't see your problem, and they're not in your language.

3
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:14,440
Take a photo and say what's wrong.

4
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:19,184
This recording runs in demo mode, with labelled stand-in photos.

5
00:00:19,184 --> 00:00:23,915
You watch the agent work: as each stage finishes, its result appears.

6
00:00:23,915 --> 00:00:29,484
What Muse Spark saw, the parts SAM 3.1 outlined, then the likely cause.

7
00:00:29,484 --> 00:00:35,104
When the evidence is ambiguous, it asks one short question instead of guessing.

8
00:00:35,104 --> 00:00:38,357
Then the diagnosis: likely causes with confidence,

9
00:00:38,357 --> 00:00:44,132
a safety level, tools, time, and the parts cost against the repair-shop price.

10
00:00:44,132 --> 00:00:50,544
The parts are masked and numbered on your own photo by SAM 3.1, not a generic diagram.

11
00:00:50,544 --> 00:00:53,142
Before step one, a short safety checklist.

12
00:00:53,142 --> 00:00:56,812
The steps stay locked until you tick every item.

13
00:00:56,812 --> 00:00:58,522
New: the live camera guide.

14
00:00:58,522 --> 00:01:05,046
Point the phone and SAM 3.1 outlines the exact part to touch, about once a second, on the live picture.

15
00:01:05,046 --> 00:01:10,496
In this demo the camera is Chromium's fake camera playing a stand-in photo.

16
00:01:10,496 --> 00:01:12,323
After each step, Check my step.

17
00:01:12,323 --> 00:01:15,505
Muse Spark compares the photo with the expected state.

18
00:01:15,505 --> 00:01:19,740
Too dark here, so it asks for the torch instead of guessing.

19
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:23,740
Retake it, and the step is verified before you move on.

20
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:24,627
Hands dirty?

21
00:01:24,627 --> 00:01:31,760
Go hands-free: each step is read aloud, and the phone listens for lanjut, ulang or cek.

22
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,693
Still broken?

23
00:01:32,693 --> 00:01:37,862
Say what happened, and the agent re-plans to the next most likely cause.

24
00:01:37,862 --> 00:01:40,500
Plan, act, verify, re-plan.

25
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:45,792
When a photo can't show a step, Muse Image draws a diagram and Muse Spark checks it.

26
00:01:45,792 --> 00:01:48,256
This one is a demo stand-in.

27
00:01:48,256 --> 00:01:56,924
Every decision is on screen: what it saw, why it asked, each photo check, each re-plan, and which Meta model did it.

28
00:01:56,924 --> 00:02:02,648
And when it's a job for a pro, one tap hands it off: a WhatsApp summary of what was found and tried,

29
00:02:02,648 --> 00:02:07,584
a search for the nearest bengkel, and a PDF with a brief for the mechanic.

30
00:02:07,584 --> 00:02:09,360
It also knows when to say no.

31
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:16,612
A rice cooker that won't heat would mean opening 220 volt internals, so the safety gate stops the guidance.

32
00:02:16,612 --> 00:02:19,071
It also works in WhatsApp, in Javanese.

33
00:02:19,071 --> 00:02:25,691
Send a photo, and the same agent replies with the marked photo, the diagnosis and a button for each step.

34
00:02:25,691 --> 00:02:28,472
A gas leak still gets a red stop.

35
00:02:28,472 --> 00:02:35,130
And with one switch, diagnosis and planning run on Muse Spark Open, Meta's open-weights model, on Baseten.

36
00:02:35,130 --> 00:02:38,028
The app shows a badge when it does.

37
00:02:38,028 --> 00:02:41,826
Under the hood: Voice Transcribe, Muse Spark to see,

38
00:02:41,826 --> 00:02:47,888
reason and check, SAM 3.1 for masks and live tracking, and Muse Image for diagrams.

39
00:02:47,888 --> 00:02:50,560
Safety is enforced in code.

40
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,524
Tukang Copilot.

41
00:02:51,524 --> 00:02:55,560
Every phone becomes a mechanic's apprentice.
